    <item>
      <title>Ordeal of the Demon King - Two New Quests</title>
      <author>- Tarnagh -</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/712592</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/712592#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">eaaf7128f93f8abe9196502d3e7dde8b2cfb18bf</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 17:15:22 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa97c7cc229e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9dae19baf40.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa97c8b8ae97.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a96fae3ed1b9.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; v2.0.0&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: New quest and reward: Horn of the Demon King&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Improvement&lt;/em&gt;: Minor improvements&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Created by &lt;strong&gt;Tarnagh&lt;/strong&gt;. Bow model and texture by &lt;strong&gt;The Hidden Yiga Clan&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Ordeal of the Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"You have faced monsters, Dragons, and gods. But have you ever stood before the Demon King himself?"&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Ganondorf stands, and he is waiting for you. Not for a battle - but for an answer. He has watched the bearer of the Master Sword from afar, counted his victories, and now he intends to find out for himself whether the hero is worth anything at all.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
This is a full quest line: dialogue, choices that stick, a duel of his choosing, and two commissions that end with weapons no one else in Hyrule can give you.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
He offers you a choice.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Kneel.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Or refuse.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Choose carefully. The Demon King does not offer his mercy twice.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Ordeal&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Those who bow before him earn something granted to almost no one: the chance to prove themselves in single combat, against an opponent he picks personally.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Survive, and he will admit - grudgingly, in his own way - that you are more than another hero clinging to a dying world. Refuse the duel, and the ordeal ends where it began, beneath his gaze.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The King's Will&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
A proven hero is a useful hero, and the Demon King has work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
His first commission sends you after the horns of three Silver Lynels, thirty of Naydra's spikes, and a horn taken from the Light Dragon herself. Bring them, and he will forge you a bow out of them, by hand, in front of you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
But do not mistake his favour for friendship. You serve his purpose for exactly as long as you remain useful.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;New: The Horn of the Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Take this. A horn of my true form. A manifestation of the doom that awaits this fragile world."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Come back to him carrying his bow and he will ask more of you - if you are willing to hear it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
This time he wants the horns of all three elemental Dragons, and two from the Light Dragon. What he makes of them is not a weapon but a piece of one: &lt;strong&gt;a shard of the form he has not yet taken&lt;/strong&gt;, fused from their elemental essence and his own dark magic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Fuse it to anything you like:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;+90 attack&lt;/strong&gt; - well past anything the base game offers&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fire in every form&lt;/strong&gt; - it sets what it strikes alight, explodes in flame, and keeps you warm.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shatters armour&lt;/strong&gt;, fells trees, and throws far,&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;On a shield: &lt;strong&gt;guard bonus, perfect-parry bonus, shield bash and counter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
It cannot be sold. Some things are not for rupees.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Features&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Demon King:&lt;/strong&gt; Ganondorf as he ought to be - imposing, calculating, merciless, and worthy of his title.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Choices that stick:&lt;/strong&gt; what you say to him is remembered across saves, and he remembers it too.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The King's Trial:&lt;/strong&gt; a duel against an opponent he chooses for you, with miasma.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Two commissions:&lt;/strong&gt; hunt across Hyrule for materials no shop sells, and watch him forge them by hand.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Two unique rewards:&lt;/strong&gt; a bow of his own making, and the Horn of the Demon King.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Begin the Ordeal&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Find him north of the Gerudo Canyon Pass, west of the Rakakudaj Shrine.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Approach, and hear his demand.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Kneel - or refuse.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;If you are still standing, decide whether to accept his trial.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Win it, and take his first commission.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Return with his bow in hand, and ask him for more.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Installation&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TKCL / TKMM:&lt;/strong&gt; import the file and enable the mod.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manual:&lt;/strong&gt; unpack the ZIP so that &lt;code&gt;romfs&lt;/code&gt; lands in&lt;br&gt;&#13;
      &lt;code&gt;atmosphere/contents/0100F2C0115B6000/romfs/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emulator:&lt;/strong&gt; place the same &lt;code&gt;romfs&lt;/code&gt; folder in the game's mod directory.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Technical Specifications&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;For developers and modders:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Host actor:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Npc_BaseCampSoldier_Hylia005&lt;/em&gt; - renamed, re-scripted, and given Ganondorf's pack. No new actor is registered.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quest logic:&lt;/strong&gt; EventFlow, in his own flowchart - branches, talk choices, pouch queries and autosaves.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Persistence:&lt;/strong&gt; six booleans appended to &lt;em&gt;GameDataList&lt;/em&gt;, with &lt;em&gt;MetaData&lt;/em&gt; resized to match so they actually reach &lt;em&gt;progress.sav&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dialogue:&lt;/strong&gt; Mals, built from genuine vanilla 1.2.0 archives.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom equipment:&lt;/strong&gt; Crystallized Ice Bow (&lt;em&gt;Weapon_Bow_166_For_Ganondorf&lt;/em&gt;), Horn of the Demon King (&lt;em&gt;Item_Enemy_39&lt;/em&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resource table:&lt;/strong&gt; every entry the mod grows is recomputed and shipped.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;The Ordeal Awaits&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;Stand before the Demon King. Prove your worth. And remember - he is the one deciding whether you deserve to live.&lt;/em&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/ordeal_of_the_demon_king_efdc3.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <category>Quests</category>
      <category>AI &amp; Events</category>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Rideable Lynels</title>
      <author>- Tarnagh -</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/663290</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/663290#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">c9c3fe2c1aebb1906325d79d06510b28ec493fd8</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:47:46 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/69cd615d6aa27.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/69c2ecc2dcebf.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/69cd613baa22b.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/69cd616c05318.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/69e21d5ff1619.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/69e2219d6fab1.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/69ee5248b48a5.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; Rideable Lynels&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bugfix&lt;/em&gt;: Fix RSDB entry&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;!-- GAMEBANANA HTML --&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h1&gt;Rideable Lynels&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;v2.4.0&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#13;
&lt;small&gt;by &lt;b&gt;Tarnagh&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/small&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;The Giant Horse is gone. In its place: a Lynel.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Ride the apex predator of Hyrule - gallop across the plains on a creature&#13;
that was never meant to be tamed. Every hoof strike, every toss of that&#13;
maned head, every burst of speed - all Lynel, all the time.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Custom-retargeted animations, thundering Lynel hoof sounds, a fully custom&#13;
stable portrait and Hyrule Compendium icon, five colour variants including&#13;
an undead Zombie skin, and three jump modes. Install, pick your variant,&#13;
and dominate the overworld on the most terrifying mount in the game.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Features&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Lynel model&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- the Giant Horse is replaced entirely by a Lynel; idle head movement and native upper body animations are preserved&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom portrait and icon&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- the stable screen and Hyrule Compendium display a custom Lynel illustration; no trace of the vanilla Giant Horse image&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Five colour variants&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Red, Blue-Maned, White-Maned, Silver, or Zombie; select in the TKMM option group before merging&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Three jump modes&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- vanilla horse arc, elevated Lynel launch, or an absurd infinite jump that clears any obstacle; select in the TKMM option group&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retargeted animations&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- leg motion mapped to the Lynel skeleton; the Lynel gallops like a horse&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lynel hoof sounds&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- thundering Lynel footsteps replace the horse audio entirely&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Boosted stats&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- HP 2000, five-star speed, full spurs&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stable-safe&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- boarding, stabling, and NPC interactions work without crashes; the Lynel behaves exactly like the Giant Horse to the game engine&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Colour Variants &lt;small&gt;(TKMM Option Group)&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&lt;table&gt;&#13;
  &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Red (Junior)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;rust-red hide&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#13;
  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Blue-Maned (Middle)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;blue skin;&lt;b&gt; DEFAULT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#13;
  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White-Maned (Dark)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;zebra-striped&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#13;
  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Silver (Senior)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;most powerful&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#13;
  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zombie&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;decayed undead skin; custom painted textures&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#13;
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Jump Variants &lt;small&gt;(TKMM Option Group)&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&lt;table&gt;&#13;
  &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Horse Jump&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;original vanilla horse jump arc&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#13;
  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Normal Lynel Jump&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;launches higher and farther; &lt;strong&gt;DEFAULT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#13;
  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infinite Jump&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;jumps over virtually any obstacle&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#13;
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Installation&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Open TKMM and add &lt;strong&gt;Rideable_Lynel.tkcl&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;In the option groups, select your colour variant and jump mode&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Merge to SD card - done&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;small&gt;To change variant later: re-select and re-merge. No save file changes needed.&lt;/small&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Compatibility&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&lt;table&gt;&#13;
  &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Game version&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;TotK 1.0.0+ (tested on 1.2.0 and 1.4.3)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#13;
  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Nintendo Switch (Atmosphère / TKMM)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#13;
  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conflicts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Any mod that modifies &lt;strong&gt;GameRomHorse00L.pack.zs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#13;
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Known Issues&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Upper body animations are too stiff in canter and gallop&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;On save reload the Lynel sometimes does not appear&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Videos&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Community Showcase &lt;small&gt;by The Hidden Yiga Clan - mod version v2.1.0&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
