    <item>
      <title>Self Recall (Switch Update)</title>
      <author>HanSoloBlaster</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/715735</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/715735#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">68388c73f43b45cdddd06eece90d88f240018836</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 04:36:01 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa22e6e49e09.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa22e6eadaf3.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa22e6f1d02d.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa22e7ddb07c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Self Recall&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Recent Fixes&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3&gt;v1.0.12&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Release Switch v1.0.12 which uses the SD card to bring back the &lt;b&gt;full 64 s recall history to Switch&lt;/b&gt; users. Note: history will be reduced to 10 seconds if your SD Card is full. You card needs at least 16 MiB of space available - 64-128 MiB is probably a safe margin.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;v1.0.13&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Batch SD history writes on Switch for reduced potential wear.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Substantially trim logging to SD card.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;v1.0.14&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Mod now works with UltraCam enabled at the same time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Description&lt;/h3&gt;Self recall lets you rewind Link through his recent traversal history. An muted background effect is applied, a golden ribbon showing your historical trail shows and animations run in reverse.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;ZL+Right-Joystick-Click (hold 1 second) to activate.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Speed&lt;/h2&gt;By default, self-recall will run in reverse at 1.25x speed. By wearing upgraded articles of clothing from the Glide set, you can increase the speed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;0 articles -&amp;gt; 1.25x&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;1 article -&amp;gt; 1.5x&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;2 articles -&amp;gt; 2x&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;3 articles -&amp;gt; 4x&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every upgraded version of the Glide Mask, Glide Shirt and Glide Tights counts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Known Issues&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Only works on version 1.2.1 of the game.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Recalling through an Ascend works - but is almost always a glitchy experience. I decided to leave it in for the novelty factor.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;On Switch, Link skips along his path at 4x speed and during fast movement at 2x.&#13;
The rest of the game stays smooth. Zero or one Glide piece gives the tested&#13;
smooth 1.25x/1.5x rates.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Driving Recall can stutter mildly at the beginning on Switch.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Recorded shirtless transitions can make Link's torso disappear.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;The camera can lose Link during fast vertical Recall or enter terrain around&#13;
climbing overhangs.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Historical pose markers along the ribbon are not included.&lt;/li&gt;4x/2x recall speed can be choppy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Link's torso, head, legs or armor may disappear during a recall.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Equipment changes are no longer tracked. (necessary for memory savings).&lt;br&gt;v1.0.9 contains more features but will crash if you enable any other mods.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Code and Detailed README&lt;/h2&gt;MIT Licensed source code and a &lt;b&gt;far more in-depth mod description available &lt;a href="https://github.com/afiaka87/totk-mods/tree/main/self-recall" target="_blank"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Disclaimer&lt;/h2&gt;Relied heavily on astra for this.</description>
