      <pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 21:40:45 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa6fc116b049.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa70f617b8a7.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa70f60a516d.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa7096d9e8bb.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa6fc825c97f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Zonai Survey v0.1.4 - The Switch Update&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;b&gt;v0.1.4 changes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mod now tested and working on Switch&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Added sophisticated/performant shader-based scan.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Reduced memory consumption from ~20 MiB to ~2 MiB.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Reduced angle of scan from 150 degrees to 100 degrees.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A &lt;b&gt;"constrained" build&lt;/b&gt; is available that reduces survey distance to 180 m and introduces a 7 s cooldown.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Other minor improvements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Description&lt;/h2&gt;Pressing &lt;b&gt;ZL + D-pad Up&lt;/b&gt; starts a Death-Stranding-inspired scan/survey that labels items in front of you by ~440m. Constrained releases introduce a 180 m survey distance cap and a cooldown lasting 7 seconds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For installation instructions and more please refer to the &lt;a href="//github.com/afiaka87/zonai-survey"&gt;README&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Limitations&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;This ONLY runs on version 1.2.1 of TotK.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;May conflict/break when other exeFS mods are enabled.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;On Switch hardware, you may notice a slight 3-5 fps dip when running the scan specifically over grass-dense areas.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Source and license&lt;/h2&gt;Zonai Survey is GPL-2.0-only. The text renderer and part of the overlay hook are&lt;br&gt;derived from &lt;a href="https://github.com/aquacluck/totk-lotuskit" target="_blank"&gt;totk-lotuskit&lt;/a&gt; by aquacluck&lt;br&gt;and its contributors. See &lt;a href="//NOTICE"&gt;NOTICE&lt;/a&gt; for full attribution.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Disclaimer&lt;/h2&gt;Sol, Fable and Astra were used during development.</description>
